Normal Python execution in this artifact environment does not have unrestricted outbound Internet, so I have **not** falsely certified live GitHub/OpenAlex/arXiv calls from the packaged program. Network collectors were tested deterministically against their expected HTTP shapes and failure semantics; the live endpoint/access assumptions were independently checked through the web research above.

### Monetization architecture

The build treats the valuable product as **derived decision advantage**, not reselling public GitHub rows.

The intended ladder is a public delayed frontier feed for distribution, an individual product with custom watchlists and architecture alerts, team/R&D workspaces with private sector graphs and APIs, and eventually enterprise/API access to historical replay, custom sectors and private-source fusion.

More importantly, it already defines the long-term moat:

```text
SIGNAL at T0
   ↓
GitGoblin says "this looks early"
   ↓
Cuntgoblin researches/builds it
   ↓
actual technical/commercial outcome
   ↓
later ecosystem trajectory
   ↓
credit/blame builders + signal types
   ↓
recalibrate priors
```

Eventually the valuable proprietary question becomes:

> **Which particular people are early and correct about which particular technical domains?**

Someone can copy the GitGoblin source code later. They cannot reconstruct years of those timestamped observations, false positives, successful predictions, identity corrections and downstream venture outcomes.

That is the part I would keep private from the start.

